I'm fine now. Thank you very much.

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:26.160
That's good to hear.

00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:28.790
So we caught 15 li'l horsies
and ten horse mackerels.

00:14:28.790 --> 00:14:30.120
That's a decent haul.

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:32.200
When did we catch so many?

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:36.120
While you were all woozy,
Ohno-<i>senpai </i>and I caught them.

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:37.790
Fishing without a reel is great!

00:14:37.790 --> 00:14:39.790
You cheeky little...

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:41.500
What are we going to do with these?

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:46.290
Well, Tsurugi can take home all the horsies...

00:14:46.290 --> 00:14:48.580
Since we managed to catch a whopper,

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:50.750
let's turn it into sashimi
and dry the rest overnight.

00:14:50.750 --> 00:14:51.950
Sashimi?

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:54.500
That's right. We've never had it that way.

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:56.750
Also, drying it over night?

00:14:56.750 --> 00:15:01.700
We take a fish fillet, soak it
in salt water, then dry it overnight.

00:15:01.700 --> 00:15:04.120
It's amazingly good when
you cook it on a <i>shichirin </i>grill.

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:06.290
The meat is so fatty, tender, and juicy.

00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:10.790
Pair it with some white rice and it's heaven.

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:12.080
I can't wait to try it!

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:13.370
That sounds amazing!

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:15.700
Right. Let's get to it.

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:16.620
Hina and...

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:18.250
...M-Makoto's...

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:20.580
Let's Cook!

00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:22.540
Let's Cook...

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:24.790
Let's start with the sashimi.

00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:26.660
First, we're going to fillet
the fish into three parts.

00:15:26.660 --> 00:15:28.040
Okay!

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:30.450
First, we're going to descale the fish.

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:33.870
We're going to peel the skin off
the <i>seigo</i>, so you can leave it for now.

00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:35.370
I see!

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:41.120
After rinsing off its scales, we're going
to cut underneath the pectoral fin

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:44.370
and cut all the way down to the ventral fin.

00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:48.790
Flip it over, cut in the same
fashion, and chop off its head.

00:15:49.910 --> 00:15:55.870
Cut from its tummy all down to
its bum and scrape out its insides.

00:15:55.870 --> 00:15:59.830
Rinse all of that off and
wipe away any excess moisture.

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:04.250
Cut from its tummy all the way down to its tail.

00:16:04.250 --> 00:16:08.000
Follow the directions of the bones
inside and cut down to its spine.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:13.040
Cut into its skin on its back,
then slice through the same way.

00:16:13.040 --> 00:16:16.500
Then cut through its tail
with the back of the knife,

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:20.620
then go back the other way
and cut the flesh from the spine.

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:22.750
Now one side is done.

00:16:24.450 --> 00:16:30.290
We'll repeat the steps for the
other side, cut out the ribs, and...

00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:32.120
We're done with our fillet.

00:16:32.120 --> 00:16:35.700
Wow, it's so pretty!
You're so amazing, Ohno-<i>senpai</i>.

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:38.580
Now, you try.

00:16:38.580 --> 00:16:41.910
Wait. Me?!

00:16:41.910 --> 00:16:44.870
Well, we all know how to do it already.

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:46.580
Ya get to practice.

00:16:46.580 --> 00:16:52.250
"Menacing"

00:16:52.540 --> 00:16:58.120
O-Okay... It's not scary... It's not scary...

00:16:58.120 --> 00:17:01.250
This is a plushie. It's not scary at all.

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:05.910
It's just a felt plushie. It's just
a very elaborate mackerel plushie...

00:17:07.950 --> 00:17:11.290
Guess it never goes right the first time.

00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:14.620
Well... This was my first time filleting a fish.

00:17:14.620 --> 00:17:16.580
What do you want from me?

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:18.330
In that case...

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:23.080
Wow! That's so fancy!

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:24.120
It looks so good!

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:26.370
Now it doesn't look so bad.

00:17:26.370 --> 00:17:28.410
You're amazing, Ohno-<i>senpai</i>.

00:17:28.410 --> 00:17:32.370
I used to eat left-over
sashimi like this all the time.

00:17:32.370 --> 00:17:34.450
That's our fishmonger's daughter for you.

00:17:34.450 --> 00:17:38.870
Then we'll go ahead and dry the other
eight overnight. Let's hurry up and eat!

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:41.160
How do you dry them overnight?

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:44.370
First, ya gotta fillet the mackerel again.

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:47.620
This method is actually easier
than splitting it into three.

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:50.290
Leave the scales but cut off its head.

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:52.370
We're actually going to
slice into its back this time.

00:17:52.370 --> 00:17:56.580
Scrape out its guts, wash out the black gunk...

00:17:56.580 --> 00:17:58.910
...and you're all set.

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:01.080
Then you're going to soak the fillet

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:05.410
in saltwater solution with about ten percent
potency for about 30 minutes to an hour.

00:18:05.410 --> 00:18:06.540
Dry off the excess moisture, and

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:07.200
"You catch it, you eat it!"
Dry off the excess moisture, and

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:10.580
"You catch it, you eat it!"
then leave it overnight in
the fridge and you're all done.

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:13.250
"You catch it, you eat it!"
Wow! I thought we were
going to let it dry outside.

00:18:13.250 --> 00:18:13.580
Wow! I thought we were
going to let it dry outside.

00:18:13.580 --> 00:18:19.040
You'd be surprised how dry
refrigerators are, so they're perfect for this.

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:21.200
And it's really hot right now,

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:23.080
so if we let them dry outside,
they could just rot.

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:25.000
Oh, I see.

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:27.910
Okay, let's hurry and finish up!

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:32.410
This will be ready tomorrow, right?
But we're off tomorrow.

00:18:32.410 --> 00:18:36.950
Then let's come here for lunch tomorrow.
Bring yer own white rice.

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:38.830
Hey, that's a great idea!

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:40.410
I can't wait!

00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:42.750
If Sayaka happens to find this...

00:18:42.750 --> 00:18:46.290
She's off tomorrow so
she'd probably drink beer...

00:18:46.290 --> 00:18:49.250
Let's not jinx ourselves...

00:18:52.660 --> 00:18:55.370
What? You're still here?

00:18:55.370 --> 00:18:58.250
Wait, what is this?! It looks so good!

00:18:58.250 --> 00:19:00.330
Is it carpaccio? No, wait!
Are you drying it overnight?!

00:19:00.330 --> 00:19:03.330
Are you eating it tomorrow?! I want some, too!

00:19:04.500 --> 00:19:07.290
It's gleaming and it looks so delicious.

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:10.370
You can actually see how
much flavor is locked in.

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:13.250
It actually dried properly. Fridges are amazing.

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:15.700
These are good to go!

00:19:15.700 --> 00:19:18.080
I'm ready over here, too.

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:22.200
Let's hurry up and eat then
scram before Sayaka shows up.

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:22.830
--Oh, so that's why you
wanted us to show up early.

00:19:22.830 --> 00:19:24.870
--How long do we cook it?
--Oh, so that's why you
wanted us to show up early.

00:19:24.870 --> 00:19:25.160
--It'll be done in less than ten minutes.
--Oh, so that's why you
wanted us to show up early.

00:19:25.160 --> 00:19:26.830
--It'll be done in less than ten minutes.
--I sort of feel bad for her...

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:28.080
--That's quicker than I thought! I can't wait!
--I sort of feel bad for her...

00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:30.660
--That's quicker than I thought! I can't wait!
--No way. She's definitely going to drink.

00:19:30.660 --> 00:19:34.450
If we leave her one after we're
done grillin' it, she won't complain.

00:19:34.450 --> 00:19:39.080
Well, maybe she won't
drink since this is for club--

00:19:39.080 --> 00:19:42.000
I knew you'd start without me!

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:43.910
I'm so glad I came early!

00:19:43.910 --> 00:19:48.160
We were just gettin' stuff ready early
so ya could eat as soon as ya got here!

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:49.500
Really?

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:51.910
You seem to have a lot with you...

00:19:51.910 --> 00:19:53.910
Oh, this?

00:19:53.910 --> 00:19:58.290
It's hot, so I bought us plenty
of drinks! Drink all you want!

00:19:58.290 --> 00:20:00.700
Wow! Thank you so much!

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:03.540
Then I guess I'll... Wait.

00:20:04.910 --> 00:20:07.700
Well, most of the drinks are for me, but.

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:10.910
Other than the tea and
orange juice, it's all beer.

00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:14.660
Ya definitely took the Sea King home last night.

00:20:14.660 --> 00:20:20.370
Oh... Because she can't drink
and drive and left her car.

00:20:20.370 --> 00:20:22.620
Ms. Sayaka, what's with the cardboard box?

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:23.950
Oh, this?

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:26.790
Ta-dah! I made my own smoker!

00:20:26.790 --> 00:20:27.830
Smoker?!

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:32.750
"Cherry smoking wood"
I figured smoking the dried fish
would be a great idea, so I brought it!

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:34.450
Wait, you made that?

00:20:34.450 --> 00:20:36.410
Yup!

00:20:36.410 --> 00:20:38.830
You see, I catch things.

00:20:38.830 --> 00:20:38.950
"Fish"
You see, I catch things.

00:20:38.950 --> 00:20:40.000
"Fish"
Wait, you mean you actually fish?

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:43.410
"Fish"
I thought I could smoke some boar or deer meat.

00:20:43.410 --> 00:20:45.540
Wait, boar meat? Deer meat?

00:20:45.540 --> 00:20:45.790
"Hunter"
Wait, boar meat? Deer meat?

00:20:45.790 --> 00:20:47.290
"Hunter"
Wait, that's what you meant?!

00:20:47.290 --> 00:20:51.290
It's really good! I'll treat you girls
the next time I catch some.

00:20:51.290 --> 00:20:55.250
Hold up a sec... This is information overload.

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:58.330
And this is exactly why ya can't get married.

00:20:58.330 --> 00:21:00.950
Leave me be!

00:21:00.950 --> 00:21:02.290
What kind of wood is that?

00:21:02.290 --> 00:21:05.950
It's cherry. They're for smoking chips.

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:07.870
I'll be taking two of these to smoke.

00:21:07.870 --> 00:21:09.580
Are these cheese and nuts?

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:11.040
They're delicious!

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:11.290
--Wow, you're really good.

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:12.830
--How long is this gonna take?
--Wow, you're really good.

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:15.250
It'll be about 30 minutes.

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:15.750
--Thirty minutes...

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:16.750
--My arm...
--Thirty minutes...

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:19.700
Man, you're so weak.

00:21:19.700 --> 00:21:21.330
We all brought rice balls.

00:21:21.330 --> 00:21:23.040
What about you, sis?

00:21:23.040 --> 00:21:25.290
An old school lunchbox with a pickled plum...

00:21:25.290 --> 00:21:26.830
Are you some old guy from the Showa era?

00:21:26.830 --> 00:21:28.500
Shut it.

00:21:29.950 --> 00:21:35.120
Now, we just need to sear
the skin a little and... all done.

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:36.950
I can't wait to eat it!

00:21:36.950 --> 00:21:38.540
I can't wait to drink.

00:21:38.540 --> 00:21:41.410
Ya beer fiend...

00:21:41.410 --> 00:21:44.160
Let's eat!

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:52.040
--So good!
--It's so good!

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:54.950
This beer is awesome!

00:21:56.160 --> 00:21:58.160
Today's haiku...

00:21:58.160 --> 00:21:59.750
"I'm gonna come back

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:01.040
to catch you again, small fry,

00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:02.870
in about three years."

00:22:02.870 --> 00:22:04.410
By Natsumi.
